REV id=P5 result=FAIL pri=1 :: Reproduced twice on isolated codex-v1-68400.sock: start `ping -t 127.0.0.1` in the pane; kill ONLY that pane's conhost; `pane get` reports host_lost with helper, PowerShell and ping. Then terminate ONLY that test PowerShell: helper exits but ping remains alive. In the second run ping was observed alive for 693 ms after shell death, then exited at 726 ms and pane get reported pane_not_found without any pane-close request. This violates P5's promise to keep a pane while its programs survive and unexpectedly ends the remaining program.
OBS ev=src:agent_detection.rs:290,src/server/host.rs:50,src/server.rs:901 :: Likely cause: tree_of starts only from helper PID and cannot traverse a missing intermediate shell; reap_host_lost sees an empty current tree and pane_exited then calls kill_tree with the previous survivor list. A single missing root is covered by the current test, but a missing intermediate node is not.
